policyFaq:
  - q: "What do the Chayce guides cover?"
    a: "The guides cover downsizing, removals costs, moving a parent, care homes, packing and storage, and settling in, grouped by topic so you can go straight to what you are trying to sort out."
  - q: "Where should I start if I am helping an older parent move?"
    a: "Start with the moving a parent and downsizing topics, then use the packing, storage and settling-in guides as the move gets closer. If you would rather talk it through, a Discovery Consultation ends with a plan, timeline and budget."
  - q: "Can Chayce help with the whole move, not just the removal?"
    a: "Yes. Chayce provides one coordinator for sorting, packing, a fully insured removal and settling in, across the UK."
  - q: "Do the guides give care, legal or financial advice?"
    a: "No. The guides are practical planning information, and Chayce does not give care, legal or financial advice. Speak to your local council or a qualified adviser for those decisions."
